cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this method, dataset or code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SKA RealTime Genomics: entropy-driven real-time learning on a genomic chain with Structured Knowledge Accumulation"
authors:
  - family-names: Mahi
    given-names: Bouarfa
    affiliation: Université Joseph Fourier
repository-code: "https://github.com/quantiota/SKA-Genomics"
license: MIT
version: d24379f
date-released: 2026-10-05
keywords:
  - genomics
  - DNA
  - Escherichia coli
  - nearest-neighbour thermodynamics
  - base-pair step parameters
  - transition probability
  - information theory
  - real-time learning
  - Structured Knowledge Accumulation
abstract: >-
  A method for studying a genome as a real-time stream. The E. coli K-12 MG1655
  chromosome (NC_000913.3) is emitted one base-pair step at a time, in
  replication order from oriC, at the DNA polymerase III fork rate. Each step
  carries a level that identifies its transition uniquely, built from the
  nearest-neighbour stacking free energy (SantaLucia 1998), the strand-dependent
  sign of tilt and the twist of the step (Olson et al. 1998; Lankas et al. 2003).
  A forward-only Structured Knowledge Accumulation learner assigns each of the
  16 base-pair transitions, and each of their 64 trinucleotide contexts, a
  constant transition probability P = exp(-|dH/H|) along the chain. These
  probability bands are sharp, stable after a short learning phase,
  independent of composition, and separate in the phase space (z, z') of the
  learner. The repository provides the validated stream, the encoding, the
  exported run and the figures.
